        "original_id": "3e38282a-1858-5f39-b56e-275b39ab24e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Publications: MetroSource, Chicago magazine, NYC Resident\n- Companies: MetroSource Publishing, Davler Media Group, tronc\n- People: Blair Boone-Migura, Wyclef Jean, Fred Hersch, Junior Vasquez\n- Organizations: Defiant Theatre\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: magazine publishing, journalism, arts\n\nFacts:\n- MetroSource is a bi-monthly gay and lesbian lifestyle magazine and business directory published in New York City by MetroSource Publishing, which is a division of Davler Media Group.\n- Chicago is a monthly magazine published by tronc.\n- In August 1999, Chicago magazine named Defiant Theatre the \"Best Experimental Theatre\" in its Best of Chicago issue.\n- Blair Boone-Migura, born James Adam Blair Boone, is a writer, professor, arts administrator, musician, and specialist in art song repertoire.\n- Blair Boone-Migura has written for MetroSource Magazine and NYC Resident.\n- Blair Boone-Migura interviewed Wyclef Jean, Fred Hersch, and Junior Vasquez for his publication work.",
